  "explains": "PhotoCard.tsx and Chart.tsx each get a new attribute. PhotoCard is imported by feed/page.tsx (/feed), photos/[id]/page.tsx (/photos/:id) and the intercepting page feed/@modal/(..)photos/[id]/page.tsx. A folder that starts with @ is a parallel slot and is not part of the URL; (..) intercepts the route one level up, so the intercepting page answers /photos/:id as well (the slot @modal does not count as a level, so (..) goes from feed to the root). Both pages of /photos/:id are one screen: the page of photos/[id] first, then the intercepting page with a chain of its own, and the intercepting route is partial (shown in place of the other only on some navigations; route_intercepted, not blocking). Chart is imported by dashboard/page.tsx and by the slot page dashboard/@analytics/page.tsx, which both answer /dashboard: one screen with two chains, the folder's own page first. Nothing else imports the two components, so /dashboard/settings and the rest are not reached.",
